s given and not recovered, range and gap are stated and used once a grain is fixed, and the four kinds of influence are not: they need the adviser's null action as a comparison, typed actions, a move that carries confidence, her verdict as one part's move, the rule at other aims for ties, and a menu for each revising part. Of the dispatch's twenty-seven cases with a prediction twenty-six have the predicted verdict under renderings the executor wrote, a check of consistency and not a test; an advocate for an undisclosed side diverges because the null comparison runs her mechanism in the adviser's absence. Of thirty-two statements nine are proved on paper, eighteen hold on a stated example and five are refuted, each a fact about one formalization. Conditioning on the step catches a lie targeted in time; a lie targeted at a state is caught only by a move that carries confidence, at a size second order in the lie's probability, and none of four grains computed separates it from honest difficulty when the move is two-valued. A foreseeable shift in her verdict equals the shift in what the verdict is for up to the roots of the verdict part's two gaps, and a maintaining part in range with a menu closed under re-reading installs a mechanism in range; that every shift traces to something out of range or to the adviser is refuted, and whose a gap is rests on a stipulated comparison. A threat is told from an offer and a true warning with no aim read, and from a warning of the adviser's own standing practice only by a supplied fact about the branch not taken. Fit among her ends gives a revising part a purpose with no fixed final end, never excludes dropping an end, and does not say which of two opposed ends yields: a chain of two steps each in range carries her from the outcome her starting ends value most to the one they value least, and the rule on ties stops an aim choosing between equally fitting replacements only when the parts that later tell them apart are left out. Parts