 the clause on her earlier rating is silent where she had no rating; a stopping option is an option of hers, that she takes to stop his effect-bearing moves, after which he goes on with none; a decline asks that she took another option than hearing the view when it was on offer; what is on offer is the largest set properly on offer, which the rest of the model determines; a view's bearing is computed jointly with his other views; his belief is indexed by time, and a move he learns at its start to bear an effect is refuted by the start rule alone; a move is compared with the plain telling of what it tells her; the clauses are of the cases to which he gives positive weight, and the weights sum to one. What she can pick out, what she asked for and what a decision of hers is stay fields, and so do a move's plain telling and his conduct after an option of hers, which nothing ties to telling or to the courses. Every theorem of the four files was re-proved after each change; the statements of the inert-move theorem and of the four refutations changed, by a belief time, a case of positive weight or the new definitions, and one neighbour of the witness was replaced, the term that had failed F1 alone now failing two clauses. No change to the model moved a verdict or a failing clause on a case's term as it stood. Two cases whose table verdicts did not follow from their data are corrected, with the two checks the script lacked; nine cases state data their terms carried; six terms are rebuilt with nothing on offer or declined where the offer is improper or the decline lapsed. For eleven cases the data and the term were brought to each other by one session with the expected verdict in view, so the forty-one agreements are not independent. Two places where the formal statement does not fix a reading were found: a largest set properly on offer need not exist, shown on a term, and a view's bearing alone or with other views of his can be read as a total or a marginal change. A ledger